    [CI][BugFix] Fix GLM-5.3-Flash PD nightly hangs and refresh baseline (#19058)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Mitigate GLM-5.3-Flash PD nightly startup hangs in
    `GLM-5.3-Flash-W8A8-130k-PD.yaml`:
    
    - Incorporate the workaround from #19049: set
    `TORCH_EXTENSIONS_DIR=/tmp/torch_extensions/glm53` in `env_common`, so
    both prefill and decode use pod-local Torch/CANN JIT build caches
    instead of the shared `/root/.cache` PVC. This mitigates suspected
    shared-cache initialization races; the exact lock-deleting process has
    not been established.
    - Add `--enforce-eager` to the prefill server command, avoiding graph
    execution on the affected prefill path.
    
    - Refresh `benchmarks.perf.baseline` from `2313.132` to `2900`, keeping
    the performance threshold at `0.97`.
    
    Companion release PR: #19059 (`releases/v0.30.0`).
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    No public API changes. Only this nightly case changes: prefill runs
    eagerly and both roles use a pod-local JIT cache. The performance
    baseline is refreshed to `2900`. Decode arguments, P/D topology,
    accuracy settings, and the performance threshold are unchanged. Prefill
    performance and cold-start behavior still need NPU validation.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - Parsed both the base and changed YAML with the repository's
    `ExternalDPConfigLoader`, resolved every rank with `RankResolver`, and
    rendered all commands with `ServerCommandBuilder`.
    - Verified both prefill API ranks receive exactly one `--enforce-eager`
    flag and all ten API ranks inherit the JIT cache variable. All eight
    decode commands, including `FULL_DECODE_ONLY`, are unchanged.
    - Compared the parsed YAML and rendered commands with the base: the
    changes are the cache environment, prefill eager flag, and performance
    baseline (`2313.132` to `2900`). Other benchmark settings and topology
    are unchanged.
    - `git diff origin/main HEAD --check`: passed.
    - Repository Ruff, codespell, typos, clang-format, and runnable Python
    checks passed. Focused codespell/typos checks also passed for the
    changed YAML. The full-tree typos check passed after rerunning with a
    single thread; the initial parallel run hit a local memory allocation
    error.
    - The full `bash format.sh ci` run could not pass on Windows:
    `/bin/bash` is unavailable to some hooks, `shellcheck` is missing, and
    `python3`-based hooks exit 9009. Markdownlint dependency setup stalled;
    `markdownlint` and `actionlint` were explicitly skipped in the remaining
    checks. No Markdown or workflow files changed.
    - Baseline refresh validation: parsed both YAML files, confirmed
    `perf.baseline == 2900` and `perf.threshold == 0.97`, and verified that
    the new commit changes only that single scalar. No local hardware
    benchmark was run for this baseline refresh.
    
    No additional test files were added: this updates the existing GLM PD
    nightly case, with focused local checks of the actual configuration
    loader and command builder. An Ascend NPU environment is unavailable on
    this Windows machine; the full affected A3 nightly run, service
    readiness, accuracy, and performance validation remain pending in CI
    before merge.
    
